A||N||6||kornholio||Parts to check for emissions testing||||1||
Z||000000||kornholio||04-23-2001||09:56 PM||||My car needs to be emission tested soon, so I was wondering what I should do to reduce the risk of failing?<BR>I replaced the spark plugs, wires, dist cap and rotor 2 years ago.<BR>Did the timing 5 months ago.<BR>The whole EGR system (tube, valve, solenoid) has been replaced along with the cat convertor within the last year and a half.<BR>The TPS and oxygen sensor are about a year old.<P>Also, when should I replace spark plug wires?  I just replaced mine 2 years ago because they were dirty.<P>Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000001||kornholio||04-23-2001||09:59 PM||||Oh yeah, forgot to mention that I get really crappy gas mileage.  I can go 200 km in the city and I fill it until I can't pump anymore at 31 litres.||||reg||1
Z||000002||kornholio||04-24-2001||09:52 AM||||^  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||ROB MAC||04-24-2001||11:02 AM||||Change the plugs every year unless you don't drive it much. Before emission test change oil + filter, plugs, air filter, rotor. Check pcv valve. If you have not changed fuel filter in last 2 years ,replace it (READ PROCEEDURE CAREFULLY FIRST!!). Step up to a higher octane gas a few days before the test. Change oil the day before test if possible. Drive the car for a half hour on your way to the test so the cat is HOT when it is tested. If cat and gas cap are in good shape you should be fine. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||ROB MAC||04-24-2001||11:10 AM||||I seem to recall the timing can't be set properly unless you first put it into sevice code mode or something has to be disconnected. I forget exactly what, but, maybe thats why you get crappy gas mileage? O2 sensor was the cause of mine.||||reg||1
Z||000005||kornholio||04-24-2001||02:28 PM||||yeah, I jumpered the plug near the cigarette lighter before I did the timing.  Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Formula88||04-24-2001||04:17 PM||||Make sure you have a 195* thermostat.  The hotter an engine runs (within reason) the better the emissions will be.  I let mine idle until the fan came on (235*) and passed emissions with flying colors.  I also don't have my EGR hooked up, but I believe the car had the cat replaced before I bought it.||||reg||1
